{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-552d2e93-fb62-4286-b752-d8af6428b854","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8bc764c367c88be","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-_i80jp0p/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E001.md","content":"# Llama Stack GA-readiness assessment\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: what exactly separates the\ncurrent Tech Preview quality of Llama Stack from the General Availability bar.\nIt produces the definitive GA-readiness assessment — a systematic inventory of\ngaps across API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error handling —\nconsolidating TP feedback scattered across support tickets, which has never\nbeen systematically collected. The assessment's output defines the definitive\nGA scope that all Llama Stack stability and hardening work is planned against.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Collect and consolidate Tech Preview feedback from support tickets and other\n  feedback channels relevant to Llama Stack distributions.\n- Assess the current API surface (LlamaStackDistribution CRD and the\n  OpenAI-compatible REST APIs exposed by the distribution) against GA stability\n  expectations; inventory every gap.\n- Assess upgrade behavior from the last two Tech Preview releases; inventory\n  breakage and missing migration coverage.\n- Assess scale limits (documented and observed) and error handling coverage\n  across the distribution's surfaces.\n- For each gap, record the current TP state, the GA bar, severity, and a\n  recommended disposition (blocking GA vs. non-blocking).\n- Produce the definitive GA scope: the consolidated, prioritized list of work\n  items the graduation effort must cover, mapped to the strategy's\n  requirements.\n- Socialize the assessment and resulting GA scope with stakeholders for\n  sign-off.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A GA-readiness assessment document exists that inventories gaps in all four\n  stated dimensions (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error\n  handling), with each gap recording current state, GA bar, and severity.\n- Every inventoried gap carries a blocking/non-blocking classification and a\n  recommended disposition.\n- A definitive GA scope list is produced, enumerating the concrete work items\n  the graduation effort must deliver, traceable to the strategy's high-level\n  requirements.\n- TP feedback from support tickets is consolidated into the assessment (no\n  feedback channel left unmined).\n- The assessment and GA scope have been reviewed and accepted by the owning\n  team and stakeholders.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)**: A GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between\n  current TP quality and GA bar (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits,\n  error handling), producing the definitive GA scope. This epic is the entire\n  deliverable of HLR-1.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":30560,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f07deed22000dae","agent_id":"ac8b09bb5b58c9e2f","session_id":"1249e1cd-8cf6-43c9-b6fd-d1e7ae430a4a","uuid":"c94dcba4-3a37-4c44-8a2a-000ca04745cc","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:09:56.906Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
