- The published Llama Stack API surface is versioned, and the versioning scheme\n  is documented.\n- A deprecation policy is published and applied: every API slated for\n  deprecation is marked with an announcement and a removal timeline consistent\n  with the policy.\n- All API-stability gaps that the GA-readiness assessment classified as\n  blocking GA are remediated or explicitly dispositioned in the GA scope.\n- Automated upgrade-path verification exists and passes for migration from each\n  of the last two Tech Preview releases.\n- The changes build and pass the existing build pipeline for the Llama Stack\n  repositories.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 (P0)**: Published API surface carries a stability guarantee:\n  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last\n  two TP releases. This epic is the entire deliverable of HLR-2.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31306,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f07deed22000dae","agent_id":"ac8b09bb5b58c9e2f","session_id":"1249e1cd-8cf6-43c9-b6fd-d1e7ae430a4a","uuid":"fbea9112-0bff-4f35-ab17-9dc5a39a5e5f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:10:05.846Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
