{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-50b6c402-f7ae-4f29-b681-f5ead1252345","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-87b2506fa1f97a01","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-_i80jp0p/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E003.md","content":"# Llama Stack production support posture\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic establishes the production support posture required for General\nAvailability of Llama Stack: documented SLO targets, a backport policy, and a\nsupported configuration matrix. Together these artifacts tell enterprise\ncustomers what behavior they can rely on, which releases receive fixes, and\nwhich configurations Red Hat supports — replacing the implicit TP posture with\nan explicit, published one.\n\nThe concrete SLO targets and the contents of the supported configuration matrix\nare informed by the GA-readiness assessment (assessed scale limits and\nerror-handling gaps); this epic's deliverables are adjusted to the definitive\nGA scope that the assessment produces.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Define and document measurable SLO targets for the GA Llama Stack\n  distribution (availability and operational behavior commitments), grounded in\n  the scale limits assessed during GA readiness work.\n- Author the backport policy: which release trains receive fixes, for how long,\n  and how security vs. functional fixes are handled.\n- Author the supported configuration matrix: the provider combinations,\n  versions, and deployment configurations that are tested and supported at GA\n  (e.g., inference provider pairings, optional RAG vector providers).\n- Remediate error-handling gaps identified by the GA-readiness assessment that\n  fall within the support-posture surface, so documented SLOs are backed by\n  actual behavior.\n- Publish the support-posture artifacts through the appropriate product\n  support channels.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- SLO targets for the GA distribution are documented, measurable, and grounded\n  in assessed scale limits.\n- A backport policy is documented, covering which releases receive fixes, the\n  support duration, and fix-type handling.\n- A supported configuration matrix is published enumerating the tested and\n  supported configurations at GA.\n- The support-posture artifacts have been reviewed and accepted by the support\n  and product stakeholders responsible for GA commitments.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-3 (P0)**: Production support posture is in place: documented SLO\n  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix. This epic is\n  the entire deliverable of HLR-3.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":31986,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f07deed22000dae","agent_id":"ac8b09bb5b58c9e2f","session_id":"1249e1cd-8cf6-43c9-b6fd-d1e7ae430a4a","uuid":"362cbbe4-34db-4b48-b9f3-c56587c7436f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:10:14.896Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
