tative requests flowing through a\n  Llama Stack distribution (functional verification passes).\n- The integration is documented, covering enablement, configuration, supported\n  scope, and limitations.\n- The integration works within TrustyAI's supported operator deployment model\n  with no experimental prerequisites.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-4 (P1)**: Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions. This epic is the\n  entire deliverable of HLR-4.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32625,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f07deed22000dae","agent_id":"ac8b09bb5b58c9e2f","session_id":"1249e1cd-8cf6-43c9-b6fd-d1e7ae430a4a","uuid":"2d77cbfd-4a79-4a59-b4e4-d37d0c0b7217","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:10:23.242Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
