{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-96ffddcf-813e-427e-8c79-3e8e4161d509","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dda17f555ba609e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-_i80jp0p/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-E006.md","content":"# Llama Stack GA documentation uplift and TP migration notes\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic uplifts the Llama Stack documentation to GA standards and adds\nmigration notes for customers moving from Tech Preview releases. It runs last:\nthe documentation must describe what was actually built — the versioned,\nstability-guaranteed API surface, the tested upgrade path from the last two TP\nreleases, the production support posture (SLO targets, backport policy,\nsupported configuration matrix), the supported TrustyAI guardrails integration,\nand default Dashboard enablement on entitled clusters.\n\n## Scope\n\nContent outline (authored through the Red Hat docs content process):\n\n- **GA overview and support posture**: what GA means for Llama Stack\n  distributions; the documented SLO targets, backport policy, and supported\n  configuration matrix, presented for users.\n- **API stability and versioning**: the versioning scheme for the published\n  API surface, the deprecation policy, and how customers should consume\n  versioned APIs.\n- **Migration notes from Tech Preview**: step-by-step migration guidance from\n  the last two TP releases, aligned with the tested upgrade path, including\n  breaking changes and required configuration updates.\n- **Safety guardrails documentation**: user-facing documentation of the\n  supported TrustyAI guardrails integration, referencing the integration docs\n  produced by that work.\n- **Getting-started and operational topics**: refresh of existing TP topics to\n  GA standards, including default Dashboard availability of Llama Stack\n  management on entitled clusters.\n- **Removal of TP-conditional language**: retire experimental/preview caveats\n  that GA status no longer excuses.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Documentation covering all topics in the content outline is published and\n  meets GA documentation standards.\n- Migration notes from the last two TP releases are documented and consistent\n  with the tested upgrade path that was implemented.\n- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented GA\n  capabilities (API versioning and deprecation policy, support posture,\n  guardrails integration, Dashboard default enablement) and reflects actual\n  behavior.\n- No Tech Preview caveats remain in topics covered by the GA uplift.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-6 (P2)**: Documentation is uplifted to GA standards, including\n  migration notes from TP. This epic is the entire deliverable of HLR-6.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33848,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f07deed22000dae","agent_id":"ac8b09bb5b58c9e2f","session_id":"1249e1cd-8cf6-43c9-b6fd-d1e7ae430a4a","uuid":"009addd3-4412-49ea-a47e-b3dee63ae92f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:10:41.667Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014"}
