ic's\n48\tscope is rewritten to match the definitive GA scope.\n49\t\n50\t## Scope\n51\t\n52\t- Introduce API versioning for the published Llama Stack surface (the\n53\t  LlamaStackDistribution CRD and the OpenAI-compatible REST APIs the\n54\t  distribution exposes), per the versioning approach selected during\n55\t  implementation.\n56\t- Author and publish a deprecation policy for the published API surface,\n57\t  including how deprecated APIs are announced and their removal timelines.\n58\t- Remediate the API-stability gaps identified by the GA-readiness assessment\n59\t  (breaking changes, unstable contracts, undocumented behaviors).\n60\t- Implement a tested upgrade path from the last two Tech Preview releases,\n61\t  covering the distribution's resources and configuration.\n62\t- Add automated upgrade-path verification so migration from each of the last\n63\t  two TP releases is exercised and passes.\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t- The published Llama Stack API surface is versioned, and the versioning scheme\n68\t  is documented.\n69\t- A deprecation policy is published and applied: every API slated for\n70\t  deprecation is marked with an announcement and a removal timeline consistent\n71\t  with the policy.\n72\t- All API-stability gaps that the GA-readiness assessment classified as\n73\t  blocking GA are remediated or explicitly dispositioned in the GA scope.\n74\t- Automated upgrade-path verification exists and passes for migration from each\n75\t  of the last two Tech Preview releases.\n76\t- The changes build and pass the existing build pipeline for the Llama Stack\n77\t  repositories.\n78\t\n79\t## HLR Traceability\n80\t\n81\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: Published API surface carries a stability guarantee:\n82\t  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last\n83\t  two TP releases. This epic is the entire deliverable of HLR-2.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bab546392563828e","agent_id":"abfbedcbafc57fb33"