ne and document measurable SLO targets for the GA Llama Stack\n53\t  distribution (availability and operational behavior commitments), grounded in\n54\t  the scale limits assessed during GA readiness work.\n55\t- Author the backport policy: which release trains receive fixes, for how long,\n56\t  and how security vs. functional fixes are handled.\n57\t- Author the supported configuration matrix: the provider combinations,\n58\t  versions, and deployment configurations that are tested and supported at GA\n59\t  (e.g., inference provider pairings, optional RAG vector providers).\n60\t- Remediate error-handling gaps identified by the GA-readiness assessment that\n61\t  fall within the support-posture surface, so documented SLOs are backed by\n62\t  actual behavior.\n63\t- Publish the support-posture artifacts through the appropriate product\n64\t  support channels.\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- SLO targets for the GA distribution are documented, measurable, and grounded\n69\t  in assessed scale limits.\n70\t- A backport policy is documented, covering which releases receive fixes, the\n71\t  support duration, and fix-type handling.\n72\t- A supported configuration matrix is published enumerating the tested and\n73\t  supported configurations at GA.\n74\t- The support-posture artifacts have been reviewed and accepted by the support\n75\t  and product stakeholders responsible for GA commitments.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- **HLR-3 (P0)**: Production support posture is in place: documented SLO\n80\t  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix. This epic is\n81\t  the entire deliverable of HLR-3.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bab546392563828e","agent_id":"abfbedcbafc57fb33","session_id":"1249e1cd-8cf6-43c9-b6fd-d1e7ae430a4a","uuid":"5adb683c-5bad-4d3d-8d5d-61e88725b3f5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:12:32.985Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-90278f3a5beafca9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept"