ioning scheme for the published\n53\t  API surface, the deprecation policy, and how customers should consume\n54\t  versioned APIs.\n55\t- **Migration notes from Tech Preview**: step-by-step migration guidance from\n56\t  the last two TP releases, aligned with the tested upgrade path, including\n57\t  breaking changes and required configuration updates.\n58\t- **Safety guardrails documentation**: user-facing documentation of the\n59\t  supported TrustyAI guardrails integration, referencing the integration docs\n60\t  produced by that work.\n61\t- **Getting-started and operational topics**: refresh of existing TP topics to\n62\t  GA standards, including default Dashboard availability of Llama Stack\n63\t  management on entitled clusters.\n64\t- **Removal of TP-conditional language**: retire experimental/preview caveats\n65\t  that GA status no longer excuses.\n66\t\n67\t## Acceptance Criteria\n68\t\n69\t- Documentation covering all topics in the content outline is published and\n70\t  meets GA documentation standards.\n71\t- Migration notes from the last two TP releases are documented and consistent\n72\t  with the tested upgrade path that was implemented.\n73\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented GA\n74\t  capabilities (API versioning and deprecation policy, support posture,\n75\t  guardrails integration, Dashboard default enablement) and reflects actual\n76\t  behavior.\n77\t- No Tech Preview caveats remain in topics covered by the GA uplift.\n78\t\n79\t## HLR Traceability\n80\t\n81\t- **HLR-6 (P2)**: Documentation is uplifted to GA standards, including\n82\t  migration notes from TP. This epic is the entire deliverable of HLR-6.\n83\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bab546392563828e","agent_id":"abfbedcbafc57fb33","session_id":"1249e1cd-8cf6-43c9-b6fd-d1e7ae430a4a","uuid":"3dd27547-326f-490c-95a8-9e56335c717e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:12:36.208Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-86db9804bb3bd9ce","permission_decisio