{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b141f35fd75ff0bd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack API stability guarantee and tested upgrade path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the GA-readiness assessment finds the API stability gaps smaller\n15\t    or larger than estimated, the stability and upgrade-path scope is rewritten to\n16\t    match the definitive GA scope before implementation proceeds.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 2\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Llama Stack API stability guarantee and tested upgrade path\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic puts a stability guarantee on the published Llama Stack API surface:\n39\tversioned APIs, a documented deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from\n40\tthe last two Tech Preview releases. It closes the API-stability gaps that the\n41\tGA-readiness assessment identifies and delivers the technical commitments that\n42\tmake the published API surface safe for enterprise customers to build production\n43\tGenAI applications against.\n44\t\n45\tThis epic's precise scope is defined by the GA-readiness assessment; the size\n46\tof the stability and hardening work is an estimate until that assessment lands.\n47\tIf the assessment's findings change the stability work required, this epic's\n48\tscope is rewritten to match the definitive GA scope.\n49\t\n50\t## Scope\n51\t\n52\t- Introduce API versioning for the published Llama Stack surface (the\n53\t  LlamaStackDistribution CRD and the OpenAI-compatible REST APIs the\n54\t  distribution exposes), per the versioning approach selected during\n55\t  implementation.\n56\t- Author and publish a deprecation policy for the published API surface,\n57\t  including how deprecated APIs are announced and their removal timelines.\n58\t- Remediate the API-stability gaps identified by the GA-readiness assessment\n59\t  (breaking changes, unstable contracts, undocumented behaviors).\n60\t- Implement a tested upgrade path from the last two Tech Preview releases,\n61\t  covering the distribution's resources and configuration.\n62\t- Add automated upgrade-path verification so migration from each of the last\n63\t  two TP releases is exercised and passes.\n64\t\n65\t## Acceptance Criteria\n66\t\n67\t- The published Llama Stack API surface is versioned, and the versioning scheme\n68\t  is documented.\n69\t- A deprecation policy is published and applied: every API slated for\n70\t  deprecation is marked with an announcement and a removal timeline consistent\n71\t  with the policy.\n72\t- All API-stability gaps that the GA-readiness assessment classified as\n73\t  blocking GA are remediated or explicitly dispositioned in the GA scope.\n74\t- Automated upgrade-path verification exists and passes for migration from each\n75\t  of the last two Tech Preview releases.\n76\t- The changes build and pass the existing build pipeline for the Llama Stack\n77\t  repositories.\n78\t\n79\t## HLR Traceability\n80\t\n81\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: Published API surface carries a stability guarantee:\n82\t  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last\n83\t  two TP releases. This epic is the entire deliverable of HLR-2.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bc0024c29b472a89","agent_id":"a22d7c25e3fb9079a"