{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a59b8e0ac60a7bff","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack GA-readiness assessment\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 1\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Llama Stack GA-readiness assessment\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis epic resolves the strategy's central unknown: what exactly separates the\n30\tcurrent Tech Preview quality of Llama Stack from the General Availability bar.\n31\tIt produces the definitive GA-readiness assessment — a systematic inventory of\n32\tgaps across API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, and error handling —\n33\tconsolidating TP feedback scattered across support tickets, which has never\n34\tbeen systematically collected. The assessment's output defines the definitive\n35\tGA scope that all Llama Stack stability and hardening work is planned against.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Collect and consolidate Tech Preview feedback from support tickets and other\n40\t  feedback channels relevant to Llama Stack distributions.\n41\t- Assess the current API surface (LlamaStackDistribution CRD and the\n42\t  OpenAI-compatible REST APIs exposed by the distribution) against GA stability\n43\t  expectations; inventory every gap.\n44\t- Assess upgrade behavior from the last two Tech Preview releases; inventory\n45\t  breakage and missing migration coverage.\n46\t- Assess scale limits (documented and observed) and error handling coverage\n47\t  across the distribution's surfaces.\n48\t- For each gap, record the current TP state, the GA bar, severity, and a\n49\t  recommended disposition (blocking GA vs. non-blocking).\n50\t- Produce the definitive GA scope: the consolidated, prioritized list of work\n51\t  items the graduation effort must cover, mapped to the strategy's\n52\t  requirements.\n53\t- Socialize the assessment and resulting GA scope with stakeholders for\n54\t  sign-off.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- A GA-readiness assessment document exists that inventories gaps in all four\n59\t  stated dimensions (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error\n60\t  handling), with each gap recording current state, GA bar, and severity.\n61\t- Every inventoried gap carries a blocking/non-blocking classification and a\n62\t  recommended disposition.\n63\t- A definitive GA scope list is produced, enumerating the concrete work items\n64\t  the graduation effort must deliver, traceable to the strategy's high-level\n65\t  requirements.\n66\t- TP feedback from support tickets is consolidated into the assessment (no\n67\t  feedback channel left unmined).\n68\t- The assessment and GA scope have been reviewed and accepted by the owning\n69\t  team and stakeholders.\n70\t\n71\t## HLR Traceability\n72\t\n73\t- **HLR-1 (P0)**: A GA-readiness assessment inventories the gaps between\n74\t  current TP quality and GA bar (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits,\n75\t  error handling), producing the definitive GA scope. This epic is the entire\n76\t  deliverable of HLR-1.\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8324dda922943b0","agent_id":"ad5f15da8fef298da","session_id":"1249e1cd-8cf6-43c9-b6fd-d1e7ae430a4a","uuid":"6d7c3d8c-a8fd-44d6-bd87-262226e2933e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:16:49.778Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a59b8e0ac60a7bff","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2a3e4d4b4da2711","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E002\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack API stability guarantee and tested upgrade path\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the GA-readiness assessment finds the API stability gaps smaller\n15\t    or larger than estimated, the stability and upgrade-path scope is rewritten to\n16\t    match the definitive GA scope before implementation proceeds.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 2\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Llama Stack API stability guarantee and tested upgrade path\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic puts a stability guarantee on the published Llama Stack API surface:\n39\tversioned APIs, a documented deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from\n40\tthe last two Tech Preview releases. It closes the API-stability gaps that the\n41\tGA-readiness assessment identifies and delivers the technical commitments that\n42\tmake the published API surface safe for enterprise customers to build production\n43\tGenAI applications against.\n44\t\n45\tThis epic's precise scope is defined by the GA-readiness assessment; the size\n46\tof the stability and hardening work is an estimate until that assessment lands.\n47\tIf the assessment's findings change the stability work required, this epic's\n48\tscope is rewritten to match the definitive GA scope.\n49\t\n50\t**Size and re-split trigger:** this epic is one logical change — the stability\n51\tguarantee on the published API surface (HLR-2's single deliverable) — so it is\n52\tnot split by sub-deliverable. Its effort is unknown until the GA-readiness\n53\tassessment lands and is provisionally at the ~2-week epic guideline. Conditional\n54\tre-split trigger: if the assessment classifies the blocking API-stability gap\n55\tset as multi-sprint work, re-split this epic along the remediation vs\n56\tupgrade-path seams (gap remediation and API versioning/deprecation in one epic;\n57\tupgrade-path implementation plus its automated verification in the other).\n58\t\n59\t## Scope\n60\t\n61\t- Introduce API versioning for the published Llama Stack surface (the\n62\t  LlamaStackDistribution CRD and the OpenAI-compatible REST APIs the\n63\t  distribution exposes), per the versioning approach selected during\n64\t  implementation.\n65\t- Author and publish a deprecation policy for the published API surface,\n66\t  including how deprecated APIs are announced and their removal timelines.\n67\t- Remediate the API-stability gaps identified by the GA-readiness assessment\n68\t  (breaking changes, unstable contracts, undocumented behaviors).\n69\t- Implement a tested upgrade path from the last two Tech Preview releases,\n70\t  covering the distribution's resources and configuration.\n71\t- Add automated upgrade-path verification so migration from each of the last\n72\t  two TP releases is exercised and passes.\n73\t\n74\t## Acceptance Criteria\n75\t\n76\t- The published Llama Stack API surface is versioned, and the versioning scheme\n77\t  is documented.\n78\t- A deprecation policy is published and applied: every API slated for\n79\t  deprecation is marked with an announcement and a removal timeline consistent\n80\t  with the policy.\n81\t- All API-stability gaps that the GA-readiness assessment classified as\n82\t  blocking GA are remediated or explicitly dispositioned in the GA scope.\n83\t- Automated upgrade-path verification exists and passes for migration from each\n84\t  of the last two Tech Preview releases.\n85\t- The changes build and pass the existing build pipeline for the Llama Stack\n86\t  repositories.\n87\t\n88\t## HLR Traceability\n89\t\n90\t- **HLR-2 (P0)**: Published API surface carries a stability guarantee:\n91\t  versioned APIs, deprecation policy, and a tested upgrade path from the last\n92\t  two TP releases. This epic is the entire deliverable of HLR-2.\n93\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8324dda922943b0","agent_id":"ad5f15da8fef298da","session_id":"1249e1cd-8cf6-43c9-b6fd-d1e7ae430a4a","uuid":"63e75eb2-ce12-4de9-a2e1-2b8179a6f04c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:16:49.780Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a2a3e4d4b4da2711","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
