{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8da41a050b272ed0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E003\n3\ttitle: Llama Stack production support posture\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Llama Stack\n6\tteam: RHOAI GenAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If the GA-readiness assessment changes the assessed scale limits\n15\t    or error-handling gaps, the SLO targets and supported configuration matrix are\n16\t    rewritten to match the definitive GA scope.\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 0\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: -1\n23\t  external_dependency: 0\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 1\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 2\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Llama Stack production support posture\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tThis epic establishes the production support posture required for General\n39\tAvailability of Llama Stack: documented SLO targets, a backport policy, and a\n40\tsupported configuration matrix. Together these artifacts tell enterprise\n41\tcustomers what behavior they can rely on, which releases receive fixes, and\n42\twhich configurations Red Hat supports — replacing the implicit TP posture with\n43\tan explicit, published one.\n44\t\n45\tThe concrete SLO targets and the contents of the supported configuration matrix\n46\tare informed by the GA-readiness assessment (assessed scale limits and\n47\terror-handling gaps); this epic's deliverables are adjusted to the definitive\n48\tGA scope that the assessment produces.\n49\t\n50\t## Scope\n51\t\n52\t- Define and document measurable SLO targets for the GA Llama Stack\n53\t  distribution (availability and operational behavior commitments), grounded in\n54\t  the scale limits assessed during GA readiness work.\n55\t- Author the backport policy: which release trains receive fixes, for how long,\n56\t  and how security vs. functional fixes are handled.\n57\t- Author the supported configuration matrix: the provider combinations,\n58\t  versions, and deployment configurations that are tested and supported at GA\n59\t  (e.g., inference provider pairings, optional RAG vector providers).\n60\t- Remediate error-handling gaps identified by the GA-readiness assessment that\n61\t  fall within the support-posture surface, so documented SLOs are backed by\n62\t  actual behavior.\n63\t- Publish the support-posture artifacts through the appropriate product\n64\t  support channels.\n65\t\n66\t## Acceptance Criteria\n67\t\n68\t- SLO targets for the GA distribution are documented, measurable, and grounded\n69\t  in assessed scale limits.\n70\t- A backport policy is documented, covering which releases receive fixes, the\n71\t  support duration, and fix-type handling.\n72\t- A supported configuration matrix is published enumerating the tested and\n73\t  supported configurations at GA.\n74\t- The support-posture artifacts have been reviewed and accepted by the support\n75\t  and product stakeholders responsible for GA commitments.\n76\t\n77\t## HLR Traceability\n78\t\n79\t- **HLR-3 (P0)**: Production support posture is in place: documented SLO\n80\t  targets, backport policy, and supported configuration matrix. This epic is\n81\t  the entire deliverable of HLR-3.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8324dda922943b0","agent_id":"ad5f15da8fef298da","session_id":"1249e1cd-8cf6-43c9-b6fd-d1e7ae430a4a","uuid":"32ebf8f0-f9c9-4d1c-8107-688c0321bbc5","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:16:55.064Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8da41a050b272ed0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept"