{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-951bebe010e9f5d5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E004\n3\ttitle: TrustyAI guardrails as supported Llama Stack integration\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: TrustyAI\n6\tteam: TrustyAI\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 5\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# TrustyAI guardrails as supported Llama Stack integration\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic promotes the TrustyAI guardrails integration for Llama Stack\n34\tdistributions from an experimental flag to a supported, documented integration.\n35\tTrustyAI already ships at GA maturity in the platform (fairness/bias metrics,\n36\tdrift detection, explainability, and guardrails); the gap is that its\n37\tguardrails integration with Llama Stack is gated behind an experimental opt-in\n38\trather than being part of the supported GA distribution surface. This epic\n39\tmakes the integration supported and documented so GA customers can rely on it\n40\tfor safety guardrails in production GenAI applications.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Promote the TrustyAI guardrails integration with Llama Stack distributions\n45\t  from experimental status to supported status: remove the experimental-flag\n46\t  gating for GA distributions and bring the integration onto the supported\n47\t  code path.\n48\t- Verify guardrails function correctly against Llama Stack distributions\n49\t  (enforcement on representative request flows through the distribution's\n50\t  safety surface).\n51\t- Author the integration documentation: how to enable and configure TrustyAI\n52\t  guardrails for a Llama Stack distribution, the supported scope of the\n53\t  integration, and its limitations.\n54\t- Align the integration with the TrustyAI operator's supported deployment\n55\t  model (TrustyAIService instances per data science project).\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- TrustyAI guardrails can be enabled for a Llama Stack distribution on the GA\n60\t  code path without any experimental opt-in flag.\n61\t- Guardrails demonstrably enforce on representative requests flowing through a\n62\t  Llama Stack distribution (functional verification passes).\n63\t- The integration is documented, covering enablement, configuration, supported\n64\t  scope, and limitations.\n65\t- The integration works within TrustyAI's supported operator deployment model\n66\t  with no experimental prerequisites.\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- **HLR-4 (P1)**: Safety guardrails via TrustyAI are a supported, documented\n71\t  integration (not an experimental flag) for GA distributions. This epic is the\n72\t  entire deliverable of HLR-4.\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8324dda922943b0","agent_id":"ad5f15da8fef298da","session_id":"1249e1cd-8cf6-43c9-b6fd-d1e7ae430a4a","uuid":"bc312fe7-bdad-4f58-8b3e-1d1419b8f618","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:16:55.813Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-951bebe010e9f5d5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
