{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f9760d542e61a1c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9014-E005\n3\ttitle: Dashboard Llama Stack management enabled by default for entitled clusters\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9014\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Dashboard Llama Stack management enabled by default for entitled clusters\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes the Dashboard's Llama Stack management experience available by\n34\tdefault on entitled clusters, removing the Tech Preview opt-in gate that\n35\tcurrently requires administrators to enable it explicitly. At GA, entitled\n36\tcustomers should see Llama Stack management in the console without any\n37\tconfiguration step. The Dashboard integrates with components through Kubernetes\n38\tCRs and its per-component feature flags and defaults (via the\n39\tOdhDashboardConfig CR), so this change is a Dashboard-side default/entitlement\n40\tchange, not new Llama Stack surface.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Change the Dashboard's Llama Stack management enablement default so that it\n45\t  is on for entitled clusters, using the Dashboard's existing feature-flag and\n46\t  default mechanism.\n47\t- Implement or verify entitlement-based gating so the experience appears for\n48\t  entitled clusters and remains hidden/unchanged for non-entitled clusters.\n49\t- Verify the Llama Stack management experience (navigation section, resource\n50\t  views, status) renders and functions against Llama Stack distributions\n51\t  without any opt-in configuration.\n52\t- Update any Dashboard-internal copy or state that still labels the Llama\n53\t  Stack experience as Tech Preview opt-in (incidental to this change; no new\n54\t  content authored).\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- On a cluster with the relevant entitlement, the Dashboard shows Llama Stack\n59\t  management with no opt-in configuration required.\n60\t- On a cluster without the entitlement, the previous behavior is preserved\n61\t  (no regression in enablement behavior for non-entitled clusters).\n62\t- The Llama Stack management views render and function against a Llama Stack\n63\t  distribution in the default configuration.\n64\t- The Dashboard change builds and passes the Dashboard's existing build\n65\t  pipeline.\n66\t\n67\t## HLR Traceability\n68\t\n69\t- **HLR-5 (P1)**: The Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for\n70\t  entitled clusters (no TP opt-in gate). This epic is the entire deliverable of\n71\t  HLR-5.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8324dda922943b0","agent_id":"ad5f15da8fef298da","session_id":"1249e1cd-8cf6-43c9-b6fd-d1e7ae430a4a","uuid":"d49a7c66-ce6b-4b00-8625-73cd6068bd02","timestamp":"2026-10-26T17:16:58.670Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f9760d542e61a1c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
